0 92 179 [
[(Occasionally a second method for making corners is more convenient.)]
[(Here we specify the slopes of the rising and falling segments \050as)]
[(always, in units per cycle\051. We then make a triangle wave with a)]
[(corner at \0500, 0\051 and another one, placed somewhere within the cycle.)]
[(The slopes of the two lines determine the second point, which will)]
[(have an x value of t/\050s+t\051 \050if we let 's' denote the rising slope)]
[(and 't' the falling one, both as positive numbers\051. The y value is)]
[(st/\050s+t\051. If we wish instead to specify the corner location \050x, y\051)]
[(\050with x in cycles, 0<x<1\051 we set s = y/x and t = y/\0501-x\051. The DC)]
[(value is y/2.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
